package:
  name: hdllint.spy
  desc: SpyGlass lint integration (`sg_shell`)
  doc: |
    SpyGlass as a lint tool. It provides deep design-rule checking across
    RTL and style families, including CDC, RDC, and methodology rules.

    What it sees: full RTL elaboration plus style/coding rules. SpyGlass
    goals range from lightweight turbo checks to full enhanced lint, so it
    implements both the `Rtl` and `Style` families.

    The backend generates a TCL script that creates a SpyGlass project,
    reads the source, runs the selected goal, and exports a text report.
    The `sg_shell -tcl_file` invocation is always used.

    Profiles map to SpyGlass goals as:

    | profile   | goal                     |
    |-----------|--------------------------|
    | `basic`   | `lint/lint_turbo_rtl`    |
    | `default` | `lint/lint_rtl`          |
    | `strict`  | `lint/lint_rtl_enhanced` |

    SpyGlass is the property of its respective owners.

  imports:
  - name: hdllint

  tasks:
  - export: Rtl
    uses: hdllint.Rtl
    desc: Runs SpyGlass RTL lint and reports normalized findings
    doc: |
      The `hdllint.Rtl` family task with `tools:` pinned to SpyGlass.
      Identical in every other respect -- same waivers, same baseline, same
      reports.

      Use this when a flow wants SpyGlass specifically; use `hdllint.Rtl`
      when it wants whatever lint tools are available.

      ```yaml
      - name: lint
        uses: hdllint.spy.Rtl
        needs: [rtl]
        with:
          top: [my_top]
          profile: strict
      ```
    with:
      tools:
        type: list
        value: [spy]

  - export: Style
    uses: hdllint.Style
    desc: Runs SpyGlass style lint and reports normalized findings
    doc: |
      The `hdllint.Style` family task with `tools:` pinned to SpyGlass.

      ```yaml
      - name: style
        uses: hdllint.spy.Style
        needs: [rtl]
        with:
          top: [my_top]
      ```
    with:
      tools:
        type: list
        value: [spy]
